##* {{RQ:Shakespeare Merchant of Venice Q1|act=V|scene=i|page=204|passage=There's not the ſmalleſt orbe [in the sky] vvhich thou beholdſt, / But in his motion like an Angell ſings, / Still quiring to the young [[eyed|eide]] Cherubins; / Such harmony is in immortall ſoules, / But vvhilſt this '''muddy''' veſture of decay [''i.e.'', the human body] / Doth groſſely cloſe in it, vve cannot heare it.}}
