###* {{RQ:Goldsmith History of the Earth|volume=I|chapter=Of Winds, Irregular and Regular|page=333|passage=Our ovvn '''muddy''' atmoſphere, that vvraps us round in obſcurity, though it fails to gild our proſpects vvith ſun-ſhine, or our groves vvith fruitage, nevertheleſs anſvvers the calls of industry.}}
