# {{lb|en|transitive}}
## To [[cover#Verb|cover]] or [[splash#Verb|splash]] (someone or something) with [[mud#Noun|mud]].
##: {{ux|en|If you '''muddy''' your shoes don’t wear them inside.}}
##* {{RQ:Forster Room with a View|chapter=Twelfth Chapter|page=200|passage=[T]hey splashed George. He was quiet: they feared they had offended him. Then all the forces of youth burst out. He smiled, flung himself at them, splashed them, ducked them, kicked them, '''muddied''' them, and drove them out of the pool.}}
## To [[make#Verb|make]] ([[water#Noun|water]] or some other [[liquid#Noun|liquid]]) [[cloudy]] or [[turbid]] by [[stir up|stirring up]] mud or other [[sediment#Noun|sediment]].
##* {{RQ:Wollstonecraft Vindication Women|chapter=Duty to Parents|page=269|passage=This is at the bottom a dictate of common ſenſe, or the inſtinct of ſelf-defence, peculiar to ignorant vveakneſs; reſembling that inſtinct, vvhich makes a fiſh '''muddy''' the vvater it ſvvims in to allude its enemy, inſtead of boldly facing it in the clear ſtream.}}
##* {{RQ:Trollope Warden|chapter=Dr. Grantly Visits the Hospital|page=82|passage=His life had hitherto been so quiet, so free from strife; {{...}} It was so hard that the pleasant waters of his little stream should be disturbed and '''muddied''' by rough hands; {{...}}}}
